# Agent Guidance: Product Documentation

When creating or organizing product documentation in this directory, refer to [README.md](./README.md) for the documentation hierarchy, artifact types, directory structure, and boundary rules.

## Key rules

- **PRDs, TRDs, user stories, and platform-level scenarios** belong under `docs/product/features/{feature}/`.
- **Surface-specific scenarios** (those whose Given/When/Then language references a specific interaction model) belong under `apps/{surface}/docs/features/{feature}/scenarios/`.
- **Step definitions** (test automation) always belong under each app's test directory, never in `docs/`.
- Every PRD must include a constitution alignment check. See `./constitution.md`.
- Every TRD must reference its corresponding PRD.
{{EXAMPLE_FEATURES_LINE}}

## When adding a new feature

1. Create `docs/product/features/{feature}/PRD.md`
2. Create `docs/product/features/{feature}/TRD.md`
3. Add user stories under `docs/product/features/{feature}/stories/` as work progresses
4. Add platform-level behavioral scenarios under `docs/product/features/{feature}/scenarios/` as acceptance criteria are defined
5. Surface-specific scenarios and step definitions are created during implementation under the relevant app

## Specification evolution

PRDs and TRDs are living documents — update in place and append to the changelog section (date, change, rationale). For evolution strategies per artifact type, consult the product-development methodology documentation (installed at `.agents/local-skills/product-development/docs/METHODOLOGY.md` or `.agents/skills/product-development/docs/METHODOLOGY.md`).
